# 1. Distributed Web Infrastructure

This setup adds load balancing and separates the database server.

## Components
- **DNS**: still maps `www.foobar.com` to the load balancer IP.
- **Load Balancer (HAProxy)**: distributes requests between 2 servers.
- **2 Web+App Servers**: serve dynamic content and execute app logic.
- **1 Database Server**: stores persistent data.

## Diagram

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  U["User"] --> D["DNS (www.foobar.com)"]
  D --> LB["HAProxy Load Balancer"]
  LB --> W1["Web+App Server #1"]
  LB --> W2["Web+App Server #2"]
  W1 --> DB[(MySQL Database)]
  W2 --> DB
```

## Notes
- **Load balancing** improves availability and scaling.
- **DB server** is separated but still a SPOF.
- No SSL, no monitoring yet.
